      "question": "Can you get SSDI and SSI at the same time?",
      "answer": "Yes, you can receive concurrent benefits from both programs if your monthly SSDI insurance payment is low enough that you still meet SSI income and resource limits under 20 CFR 416.1121 and 20 CFR 416.1205."
    },
